# Every file under third_party/, stored unmodified as its upstream publishes it (the CNCF third-party licence policy's
# "designated third-party folder"). tools/check-third-party.sh (the `licenses` CI job) fails on a file missing from
# this list, a listed file that is missing or whose sha256 differs, and a licence that is neither on deny.toml's
# allowlist nor named with an exception here. To update a file: replace it with the upstream file, unmodified, and
# change its line (hash and source) in the same commit.
#
# Fields, whitespace-separated, one file per line:
#   path        relative to third_party/
#   sha256      of the file as upstream serves it at `source`
#   licence     one SPDX identifier
#   source      the exact upstream URL the file is byte for byte (a pinned commit, never a branch)
#   exception   `-` when the licence is allowlisted; else the CNCF exception id (exceptions.json), or `none`
#               for one not granted yet (a known gap, not an approval)
#
# The Public Suffix List: MPL-2.0, no CNCF exception yet; the request for one is not made.
